==================================================================
DAY 52 - PART A: THEORY
TLS Certificates and cert-manager
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. TLS AT THE INGRESS
---------------------
Users connect with HTTPS to the ingress controller (or cloud LB),
which terminates TLS using a certificate stored in a kubernetes.io/tls
Secret (Day 19 Step 8, made by hand with openssl). Certificates
expire (Let's Encrypt: 90 days). Renewing by hand across many apps
doesn't work.


2. cert-manager
---------------
A controller that issues and RENEWS certificates automatically.
CRDs:
  Issuer / ClusterIssuer   where certificates come from:
                           SelfSigned, CA (your own CA), ACME (Let's
                           Encrypt, ZeroSSL), Vault, cloud CAs
  Certificate              "I want a cert for these DNS names, put it
                           in Secret X"; renewed before expiry
  CertificateRequest, Order, Challenge   internal steps (ACME)


3. INGRESS SHORTCUT
-------------------
Annotate an Ingress; cert-manager creates the Certificate for you:
  metadata:
    annotations:
      cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer: letsencrypt-prod
  spec:
    tls:
    - hosts: [shop.example.com]
      secretName: shop-tls


4. ACME (LET'S ENCRYPT) CHALLENGES
----------------------------------
Let's Encrypt must verify you control the domain:
  HTTP-01  it fetches http://<domain>/.well-known/acme-challenge/<token>
           cert-manager serves this via a temporary Ingress. Needs the
           domain to resolve publicly to your ingress.
  DNS-01   you prove control with a TXT record (cert-manager uses
           Route 53/Cloudflare/Azure DNS APIs). Works for private
           clusters and wildcards (*.example.com).
Use the STAGING server first (rate limits on production).
In a local kind lab you can't do public ACME, so we use a private CA.


5. INSIDE THE CLUSTER
---------------------
cert-manager also issues certs for internal mTLS, webhooks, and
databases. Service meshes (Istio, Linkerd) automate pod-to-pod mTLS.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- TLS lives in kubernetes.io/tls Secrets used by Ingress.
- cert-manager: Issuer -> Certificate -> Secret, auto-renewed.
- HTTP-01 needs public reachability; DNS-01 works anywhere.
